## Performance Analysis

| Algorithm | Time Complexity | Space Complexity |
|------------|----------------|------------------|
| Minimax | O(b^d) | O(d) |
| Alpha-Beta Pruning | O(b^d) | O(d) |
| Heuristic Alpha-Beta | O(b^k) | O(k) |
| MCTS | O(N × Simulation Length) | O(N) |

Where:

- b = branching factor
- d = search depth
- k = depth limit
- N = number of simulations

---

## Conclusion

The implemented algorithms successfully determine optimal moves for Tic-Tac-Toe game states.

Minimax and Alpha-Beta Pruning guarantee optimal decisions, Heuristic Alpha-Beta improves computational efficiency through evaluation functions, and Monte Carlo Tree Search provides a simulation-based alternative suitable for larger search spaces.

This project demonstrates the practical application of adversarial search techniques in Artificial Intelligence.
